;; (write-ahead)"): a run of one test, its subject, judged against another test's reference by the
;; level's own judge, which must say it does not pass. java.check/plan writes the reference's expected
;; results into the subject's plan (control lines: its first action's status and stdout digests, its
;; class files' digest); bin/java-check judges the subject's own run a second time against them, by
;; run_actions' judge (interp, compiled) and classes_verdict (classes), under the control's id; and
;; java.check/report (and bin/java-check --essential-compiled) fail the run when a control passes (the
;; judge passes what differs: 2026-10-31's two judges) or did not reach the judge while its subject ran.
;; GTS84 (a): at diagnostics (java.check/plan-diag: control-diag CID EXIT GOLDEN) the subject's actions up to its
;; first golden one judged again by diag_judge, that action's output against the reference's golden file
;; (diag_golden) and its status against the reference's; at print (control-print CID REF) java.print/judge
;; judges the subject's printed run by the steps' own comparisons against the reference's original (forms: F2
;; against the reference's F1; text: the full print against its source; classes: the printed class files'
;; digest, then the trees, against the reference's), and the control differs only when every step does; a
;; control whose reference was not printed in the run (a selection) is left.
